This directory is where vst-ace looks for real Microsoft runtime DLLs, and it
ships empty because those files are not ours to redistribute.

Some plug-ins import a Microsoft C or C++ runtime whose objects cannot be
stubbed -- iostreams and locale have vtables and internal state -- so the host
maps the genuine DLL instead. Without it those plug-ins load with several
hundred imports bound to a generic stub and fail, usually far from the cause.
Everything else works with this directory empty, which is how it ships.

  runtime/     x86-64 DLLs, for peload, peserve, pestudio and dwstudio
  runtime32/   i386 DLLs, for peload32

Both are searched next to the installed binaries, so the files go straight in
here with no configuration. What is wanted is the Visual C++ 2013
redistributable -- msvcp120.dll, and msvcr120.dll beside it for the 32-bit
loader -- in the matching width. Wine's builds of the same DLLs are not a
substitute: they are compiled against Wine's own ntdll and fault during their
own startup.

PELOAD_DLL_PATH overrides this search if the files live somewhere else.
